[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (8 issue(s)) — The implementation partially addresses the prescribed root cause — ContentstackProvider correctly switches from useMemo to useState and adds an updateContent callback — but two critical layers are missing: (1) the Contentstack SDK `options` object has no `live_preview` configuration, so the SDK never initializes live preview and `onEntryChange` will never fire; (2) no `includeDraft` propagation through the service layer means draft content can never be fetched even if the callback fires. Additionally, the onEntryChange callback blindly casts SDK payload as Partial<IContentstackContent> without mapping the entry to the correct content-type key, which would corrupt state. The diff also includes unnecessary changes to IContentCard (previewId/isPreview/previewTimestamp) and ContentstackLink (previewMode prop) that are not part of the prescribed minimal fix and violate the concision requirement. Zero unit tests were added. Verdict: changes_requested.

