[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (8 issue(s)) — The Live Preview feature (AMSD-2041) is completely unimplemented. None of the prescribed minimal fixes from the Root Cause Analysis were applied. (1) The Contentstack Stack `options` object has no `live_preview` config block — the SDK will never process preview data. (2) The `ContentstackContext` is a bare `createContext` with no Provider component, no `useState`, no `useEffect`, and no `onEntryChange` subscription — the 236+ consumers of `useContent` will always receive static SSR content. (3) The `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` SDK is not installed. (4) No `live_preview` fields were added to query/entry config interfaces. (5) No `includeFallback()` calls exist in the query chain. (6) No `pages/api/preview.ts` route exists for Next.js draft mode. (7) No `context.preview`/`previewData` forwarding in page components. (8) Zero unit tests for the feature. Every single acceptance criterion is unmet: draft content cannot be displayed (AC1), real-time updates are impossible (AC4, AC5), platform-specific preview cannot work (AC3), and even basic published content flow through a reactive provider is absent. This is a non-implementation, not an incomplete or over-engineered one.

